{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{#
  This page is the redirect target for every form on the site (see the
  `action="/thank-you/"` attribute on the quote, contact, and newsletter
  forms). A real page load here — rather than an inline JS success message —
  is what lets conversion-tracking pixels fire reliably, which matters the
  moment you start running paid ads (Google Ads, Meta/Facebook Ads, LinkedIn
  Ads, etc.). Two conversion snippets are stubbed out below, commented out.
  Uncomment and fill in your own IDs when you're ready to run ads; leave them
  out entirely if you aren't.
#}

<section class="page-hero" style="min-height:56vh;display:grid;align-items:center;">
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center;">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Message received</span>
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-800);">Thank you — we'll be in touch soon.</h1>
    <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:52ch;margin:var(--space-4) auto var(--space-6);">
      Your message has reached our team. Expect a reply from a real person
      within one business day — sooner for urgent projects.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn--accent" href="/">Back to home {{ icon('arrow-right', 14) }}</a>
  </div>
</section>

{#
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  AD CONVERSION TRACKING — uncomment what you use, drop in your real IDs.
  Both snippets fire once, on this page's load, which only happens after a
  genuine form submission (never on a page refresh of the form itself).
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Google Ads conversion (requires gtag.js already loaded site-wide — add
  that base snippet to base.njk's <head> first, then this fires the event):

  <script>
    gtag('event', 'conversion', {
      'send_to': 'AW-XXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX' // replace with your Conversion ID/label
    });
  </script>

  Meta (Facebook) Pixel conversion (requires the base Pixel snippet already
  loaded site-wide in <head>):

  <script>
    fbq('track', 'Lead');
  </script>
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#}
